cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DrosoTracker, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "DrosoTracker"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained web application with a self-calibrating thermal model for husbandry
  scheduling and lifespan analysis in Drosophila melanogaster. It predicts development with a
  thermal-summation model recalibrated by regression on primary data (T0 = 11.78 °C,
  DD = 116.38 °C·days, R² = 0.997), offers an optional two-level calibration (laboratory
  wild-type and per genotype) driven by user observations, schedules husbandry tasks, and
  analyses adult cohort survival with the Kaplan-Meier estimator, the log-rank test and
  Schoenfeld's sample-size formula.
type: software
license: MIT
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-10"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gersonasti/Drosotracker"
url: "https://drosotracker.maimonides.edu"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21867404"   # concept DOI: always resolves to the latest archived version
keywords:
  - Drosophila melanogaster
  - thermal-summation model
  - development scheduling
  - laboratory software
  - Kaplan-Meier survival analysis
  - experiment planning
